          <change when="2025-04-29T06:13:45-04:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/james.cowey">Finalized - Ready.</change>
          <change when="2025-04-28T03:45:36-04:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/gclaytor">Vote - AcceptText - Voting through because the reading is an improvement over the ed. pr., but the correction would better be presented with comment, since Pet(h)eus is a heavily Fayumic name. I see some examples with this spelling, however, in apparently Hermopolite texts: https://papyri.info/ddbdp/p.ryl;2;201 and https://papyri.info/ddbdp/sb;6;9595</change>
          <change when="2025-04-25T11:27:34-04:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/james.cowey">Vote - AcceptText - Seems like a better suggestion to me for the reading of the name. Τελεύτος appears only once in CE papyri here in this text - see https://www.trismegistos.org/namvar/68924. </change>
          <change when="2024-12-21T17:47:32-05:00" who="http://papyri.info/editor/users/costasbala">Submit - Correction of the patronymic in l. 4</change>
